Windows Registry Editor Version 5.00

; ============================================================
; DWM Flip Model Tweaks (Hardware Legacy + Composed Independent)
; Windows 11 Gaming Optimization Guide
; Source: FR33THYFR33THY/Ultimate
;   - 8 Advanced/12 Hardware Legacy Flip.ps1
;   - 8 Advanced/13 Hardware Composed Independent Flip.ps1
; Copyright FR33THY (MIT)
; ============================================================
; Tier: Advanced
;
; Two related DWM (Desktop Window Manager) tweaks that influence the
; presentation path the OS chooses for borderless / fullscreen apps.
; Complementary to our existing MPO disable.
;
;   ForceHWComposed = 1
;     Forces DWM to use hardware-composed presentation when available.
;     Pairs with disable-mpo to avoid the OS falling back to a software
;     compositor under multi-monitor scenarios.
;
;   ForceHWLegacy = 1
;     Re-enables the legacy presentation path on systems where modern
;     DWM negotiation is unstable (rare; documented for completeness).
;
; If you've already run disable-mpo.ps1, applying this is usually
; redundant. If you haven't, this can help stutter in some
; borderless-window setups.
;
; Pair: revert-dwm-flip-model.reg
; ============================================================

[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Microsoft\Windows\Dwm]
"ForceHWComposed"=dword:00000001
"ForceHWLegacy"=dword:00000001
